Negative control for the overlay's hand-off back to the page (`R6-2b` · `R6-15`).

Hands the page back the moment the JOURNEY says it is authenticated, instead of
waiting for the ACTIVE SESSION the guard reads. That is the R6 P0 verbatim: the
store promotes the session a beat later, so the guard that sent the visitor here
still sees a guest, re-targets this very overlay, vue-router discards that as a
redundant navigation — and the close never lands. The overlay closes, the url
stays on `/auth/`, and from there every add-session click is a silent no-op.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the overlay hand-off spec — resolve must not emit `close` until the active
session reports authenticated.

diff --git a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/pages/overlays/auth.vue b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/pages/overlays/auth.vue
--- a/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/pages/overlays/auth.vue
+++ b/playgrounds/labs-nuxt/app/pages/overlays/auth.vue
@@ -88,7 +88,6 @@
